+## Wild-estimate / speculative quantification requests
+Asked for `create-stack`: a stack chart estimating "the amount of life in the
+universe" (quality × quantity) across the entire Big Bang→heat death timeline
+— a request with no real data behind it at all, just an invitation to guess.
+Handled by making the guessing itself the transparent, inspectable part: a
+reveal-panel table of the actual quantity/quality numbers used per layer with
+one-line justifications, explicit "this could reasonably be zero/disagree
+with this" caveats on the shakiest ones, and a toggle to remove the most
+speculative layer entirely and see the alternative. No direct feedback yet
+(first turn), but this fits the existing "mechanism as opt-in reveal" and
+"concrete over abstract" preferences extended to a case with no ground truth
+— worth confirming whether the exposed-assumptions-table approach is what
+lands, versus e.g. wanting adjustable sliders instead of a static table.
